    "created_at": "2021-07-15T15:41:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-15T15:41:59Z",
    "body": "I don't think gecko distinguishes between a \"scriptable\" vs. \"messageable\" popup window created with `window.open`. We always (unless `noopener` is set) open a window with a same-origin initial about:blank document, and then navigate it to the final requested URL. With the new BFCache approach we're taking with Fission, all BCGs with multiple toplevels have BFCache blocked, and we don't treat them differently.\r\n\r\nThe existing behaviour with Fission disabled is to allow caching documents which are visible to other webpages, so long as the `unload` listener isn't present. This is unfortunately quite visible to webpages and can have some quite strange impacts, which is one of the reasons we're moving away from it.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
